  "statement": "Let $S$ be a Noetherian scheme, let $U\\to S$ be separated, locally of\nfinite type and quasi-compact, and assume that $U_1\\cap U_2$ is dense in\n$U$. Then the constructed map $U_1\\cap U_2\\to W$ has dense image.",
  "proof": [
   {
    "text": "By [lemma-nagata-two-open-density-transport] the induced open immersion\n$j_W\\colon U\\to W$ has dense image. The map $U_1\\cap U_2\\to W$ is the\ncomposite of the inclusion $U_1\\cap U_2\\subseteq U$, which has dense image\nby hypothesis, with $j_W$. By continuity of $j_W$, the closure of the image\nof $U_1\\cap U_2$ contains $j_W(U)$, whose closure is $W$; hence the\ncomposite has dense image.",
    "uses": [
     "lemma-nagata-two-open-density-transport"
    ],
    "elementary": false
   }
  ],
  "note": "the current blueprint (main-20261023, weil-conjectures-blueprint c9b5f3ad18) states or proves this differently; the node is proved in Lean: recorded 2026-10-23, not reopened"
